    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "No. 7 Pound Street is a well located two-bedroom townhouse, ideally situated in a convenient town-centre location. The property offers good living accommodation throughout, making it an ideal choice for those seeking a home in the heart of the town or an investment opportunity.\nThe ground floor comprises an entrance hall, sitting room with open fireplace, living room with stove, kitchen and bathroom. Upstairs there is a landing and two double bedrooms. Externally, the property benefits from a concrete rear yard, small storage shed, rear garden and vehicle access from the back. Services: Mains water, mains sewerage, electric radiators, stove, Sky and broadband availability. Edgeworthstown is a vibrant and growing town with a good range of amenities close at hand, including two national schools, supermarkets, a state-of-the-art library, the new Co:worx hub, restaurants and a variety of local services. The town is also well served by rail, with regular services connecting Edgeworthstown with Dublin and Sligo.\n\nACCOMMODATION\nENTRANCE HALL: 1.0m x 2.0m\nSITTING ROOM: 2.2m x 3.2m Includes open fireplace.\nLIVING ROOM: 2.3m x 4.3m Includes stove.\nKITCHEN: 2.6m x 2.5m\nFIRST FLOOR LANDING\nBEDROOM ONE: 4.3m x 2.3m Double bedroom.\nBEDROOM TWO: 2.7m x 2.0m Double bedroom.\nBATHROOM: 1.5m x 2.2m\n\n"
